      </li>
      <li class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">What is salary sacrifice super and is it worth it?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">Salary sacrifice into super means redirecting a portion of your pre-tax salary into your super fund as additional concessional contributions. The contribution is taxed at 15% inside the fund instead of your marginal tax rate (up to 47%). For anyone in the 32.5% tax bracket or above, salary sacrifice almost always saves money. Use CalcPhi's <a href="/australia/salary-sacrifice-calculator/">Salary Sacrifice Calculator</a> to see the exact numbers for your salary.</p>
